<script>
  import Proof from '$lib/components/proof.svelte';
</script>

Let $\X$ and $f$ as in [%full](/statements/jump-diffusion-ito), and further impose $f$ is bounded.
Then the composition $f(\X)$ is a special semimartingale with the decomposition as in [](tag:eq-jump-diffusion-generator).

<Proof>

Seeing as $f$ is bounded, [Lemma I.4.24](/citations#jacod2003) tells us that $f(\X)$ is a special semimartingale.
By [Proposition I.4.23](/citations#jacod2003), it is then the case that the following term is locally integrable.
$$
  \Big( f(\X_-+\id_\vecSpace) - f(\X_-) - \Der f(\X_-) \cdot \trunc \Big) \ast \jumpMeas^\X_t
$$
By our discussion above, this suffices to conclude [](tag:eq-jump-diffusion-generator).

</Proof>
